<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.patched.decommission.plist — detached agent-decommission daemon (PAT-1109).

  Ships inside the bundle as a DORMANT template — never listed in
  install.sh's LAUNCHDAEMONS array, never auto-bootstrapped at install time.
  The ONLY thing that ever copies this into /Library/LaunchDaemons and
  bootstraps it is endpoint/patched-fetch-config.sh's PATCHED_DECOMMISSION_GATE
  block, and only after it has independently re-verified the signed
  decommission directive at the point of action (config hash-pin back to an
  Ed25519-verified commit, tenant binding, anti-rollback, mode/expiry
  sanity — see that block for the full rule set).

  ⚠️  THE MOST DESTRUCTIVE PATH IN THE PRODUCT. This daemon removes the
  Patched agent from this Mac, irreversibly, optionally including
  credentials and the local queue (--purge, recorded in
  decommission-info.json, not read from this plist). There is no channel
  left to correct a mistake once it runs to completion. Strictly more
  destructive than the existing app-removal daemon
  (com.patched.uninstall-check.plist / endpoint/patched-uninstall.sh), which
  is still gated and carries its own do-not-ship warning for a narrower
  blast radius (one managed third-party app, never the agent itself).

  CLEARED FOR CUSTOMER ENDPOINTS, 2026-08-14, PAT-1344. This path previously
  carried a do-not-ship-until-reviewed warning; the review it named had
  never actually been performed. It has now been run for real — the whole
  decommission path, macOS and Windows, in front of three independent
  non-author reviewers, with every finding checked against the code and the
  one real defect fixed in the same change. Full record in the header of
  patched-decommission.sh. This is the compensating local review, not an
  enforced upstream gate: the patched/non-author-review rulesets are
  disabled estate-wide.

  RunAtLoad only, no StartInterval: it runs once per boot, and finishing its
  work is what removes it — see patched-decommission.sh's SELF-CLEANUP
  section, which is deliberately the last thing that script does. If
  interrupted (sleep, power loss, kill -9), the NEXT boot re-runs it,
  because every step it performs is idempotent — the endpoint-uninstall.sh
  and macos-uninstall.sh copies staged alongside it are themselves safe to
  re-run — and self-cleanup only ever happens after both have completed.

  ProgramArguments' path is a fixed constant, not templated per-tenant: it
  MUST match PATCHED_DECOMMISSION_GATE's DECOMMISSION_DIR default in
  endpoint/patched-fetch-config.sh exactly, since the gate stages
  patched-decommission.sh at that exact path before bootstrapping this
  plist unmodified.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.patched.decommission</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>/Library/Application Support/Patched/.decommission/patched-decommission.sh</string>
  </array>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Root is required for launchctl bootout of other daemons, and for
       macos-uninstall.sh / endpoint-uninstall.sh's own root checks. -->
  <key>UserName</key>
  <string>root</string>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/var/log/patched-decommission.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/var/log/patched-decommission.log</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin</string>
  </dict>

  <!-- Throttle restarts on repeated crashes within the same boot session. -->
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>60</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
